Closure Lab is a new, AI-assisted engineering iteration of the author's earlier
self-study programming exercises. It is not a claim that the original exercises
already contained a text parser, CLI, explicit continuation machine or release tooling.

The author confirmed that the supplied historical code was independently written.
Some supplied comments still resemble teaching instructions ("please complete",
"in class", and TODO skeletons); the original source files and compiled artifacts
are deliberately not redistributed. If a third-party source is later identified,
its contribution and license must be reviewed before adding it to this repository.

The published implementation, tests and documentation were written for this project.
Standard language concepts such as lexical scope, closures, S-expressions and the
call-by-value Z combinator are described as concepts, not claimed as inventions.

No .exe, .pdb, .class, IDE project metadata, original archive, personal document,
access token or private historical path belongs in the published project.
